## Multiple Type Parameters

### Functions with Two Type Params
```xiom
fn to_pair[T, U](a: T, b: U) -> (T, U) {
  return (a, b);
}

fn transform[T, U](value: T, f: fn(T) -> U) -> U {
  return f(value);
}
```

### Functions with Three or More
```xiom
fn zip_three[A, B, C](a: &Vec[A], b: &Vec[B], c: &Vec[C]) -> Vec[(A, B, C)]
  requires: a.len() == b.len();
  requires: a.len() == c.len();
{
  var result = Vec[(A, B, C)]();
  for i in 0..a.len() {
    result.push((a[i], b[i], c[i]));
  }
  return result;
}
```

### Independent Constraints
```xiom
fn compare_and_display[T: Ord + Display, U: Display](a: T, b: U) -> Str {
  let cmp = if a > b { "greater" } else { "less or equal" };
  return a.to_str() + " is " + cmp + " than " + b.to_str();
}
```

### Structs with Multiple Type Params
```xiom
pub type Dictionary[K: Hash + Eq, V] = {
  buckets: Vec[Vec[(K, V)]];
  size: Int;
}

pub type Cache[K: Hash + Eq, V] = {
  map: Dictionary[K, V];
  max_size: Int;
  hits: Int;
  misses: Int;
}
```

